:["DepthFive"]}],"scope":"Let $\\mathrm{IMM}_{n,n}$ be the $(1,1)$ entry of the product of $n$ independent $n\\times n$ variable matrices. The formalization proves that, over every characteristic-zero field, syntactically homogeneous depth-five $\\Sigma\\Pi\\Sigma\\Pi\\Sigma$ circuits computing this polynomial require at least $n^{\\sqrt n/400}$ gates for all sufficiently large $n$, with a threshold independent of the field. Arbitrary bottom support, finite fan-in and fan-out, and sharing are allowed.\n\nIt also gives, over every field and for $n\\ge2$, circuits with at most $n^{\\sqrt n+4}$ gates. These are the lower and upper bounds selected from the paper.","title":"Homogeneous depth-five lower bounds for iterated matrix multiplication","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/135.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":null,"reading":"reading:b0e0f8edd91be96fac415c39","source_term":"MATCHES","state":"all"},{"definitions_to_check":"`Depth5Circuit` is a bespoke structure (leaf/bottom/lower/middle/upper/output arrays with `bottomHomogeneous`, `middleHomogeneous`, `outputHomogeneous` degree-equality fields) and `circuitSize` counts all nodes; homogeneity is syntactic and the model charges nodes, not wires","gap":null,"note":"None.","reading":"reading:c4c234e51f502f842d2e040b","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:b0e0f8edd91be96fac415c39","reading:c4c234e51f502f842d2e040b"],"state":"agree"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"c0851ae4ba3e12b1170cd4cdae33b48fae15d9a0","authors":[{"handle":"carlost